# Applies to every image built here — api, worker, email_worker, beat and web
# all use the repo ROOT as their build context.
#
# This file is not a size optimisation, it is load-bearing. Without it,
# `COPY apps/web/ ./` in apps/web/Dockerfile.prod copies the HOST's
# apps/web/node_modules straight over the node_modules installed in the deps
# stage — replacing a Linux install with whatever the developer's machine
# happens to have, native binaries for the wrong platform included.

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image, never copied in.
**/node_modules

# Build output
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/out

# Python bytecode and local virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv

# VCS and editor noise
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Local env / secrets. .env.prod is supplied to containers via env_file at
# RUN time, and must never be baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env.local

# Caches no runtime image needs
**/.pytest_cache
**/coverage
**/.pnpm-store
